# Documentation installed into /usr/share/doc/tab-atelier{,-headless}/.
#
# ONE list, two packagings. The deb reads it by hand (cargo-deb needs literal
# asset entries in Cargo.toml, so it cannot read this file) and a test asserts
# the two agree — add a line here and `docs_shipped_by_every_packaging` tells
# you if the deb side is missing it. The Arch PKGBUILD calls
# scripts/install-docs.sh, which reads this directly.
#
# The Arch package fell behind exactly because there was no such list: the deb
# gained the handbook and nobody thought to touch the PKGBUILD.
#
# Paths are relative to the repository root. Blank lines and # comments are
# ignored. LICENSE is deliberately absent: Debian wants it in
# /usr/share/doc/<pkg>/, Arch in /usr/share/licenses/<pkg>/, so each packaging
# places it itself.
README.md
assets/openapi.yaml
docs/self-organization.md
docs/fleet-playbook.md
